1838
00:10:17,017 --> 00:10:19,227
<i>It's time to beef up my strategy!</i>

1839
00:10:19,417 --> 00:10:20,717
I know!

1840
00:10:20,717 --> 00:10:23,687
Why don't we all go out somewhere 
together on our next day off?

1841
00:10:23,797 --> 00:10:25,907
Oh, that sounds wonderful.

1842
00:10:25,907 --> 00:10:30,147
I'm sorry, but I'm supposed to return 
to my parents' house on days off.

1843
00:10:30,377 --> 00:10:35,267
Then, let's plan something 
when it suits all of our schedules.

1844
00:10:35,267 --> 00:10:36,837
Yes, let's.

1845
00:10:36,837 --> 00:10:39,667
You're spending the day off 
with your family, Maria-san?

1846
00:10:39,667 --> 00:10:41,247
You must be looking forward to that!

1847
00:10:41,327 --> 00:10:42,207
Huh?

1848
00:10:42,797 --> 00:10:44,867
Y-Yes...

1849
00:10:54,017 --> 00:10:57,567
Real fields on real farms are so incredible!

1850
00:10:57,567 --> 00:11:00,257
The size and scale 
of them don't even compare!

1851
00:11:00,257 --> 00:11:03,437
Why did we have to come 
to a place like this on our day off?

1852
00:11:04,587 --> 00:11:05,827
Sister?

1853
00:11:05,827 --> 00:11:07,437
Why are you dressed like that?

1854
00:11:09,347 --> 00:11:11,477
The fields! I'm going to the fields!

1855
00:11:11,477 --> 00:11:13,767
The fields? But they're right here.

1856
00:11:13,767 --> 00:11:15,137
Not these!

1857
00:11:15,137 --> 00:11:18,757
I want to go to a real farm and see a big field!

1858
00:11:18,757 --> 00:11:20,157
Huh? Why?

1859
00:11:20,387 --> 00:11:22,007
Well, of course...

1860
00:11:22,007 --> 00:11:24,747
so I can become a skilled farmer if the need arises!

1861
00:11:25,527 --> 00:11:28,367
I don't even know where to start...

1862
00:11:29,057 --> 00:11:34,387
I'm disguised as a merchant's daughter 
so no one will know I'm a noble.

1863
00:11:34,387 --> 00:11:38,217
So let's get this undercover observation started!

1864
00:11:38,217 --> 00:11:39,477
Right, right...

1865
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:12,297
The undercover plan worked perfectly!

1866
00:12:12,697 --> 00:12:13,677
Huh?

1867
00:12:13,837 --> 00:12:15,097
Is that...

1868
00:12:15,097 --> 00:12:17,887
I believe that's Maria Campbell-san's hometown.

1869
00:12:17,887 --> 00:12:19,417
That's Maria's town?!

1870
00:12:19,417 --> 00:12:21,607
If we go there now, maybe we could see her!

1871
00:12:21,607 --> 00:12:24,357
What? It'd be rude to show up unannounced!

1872
00:12:24,357 --> 00:12:26,747
It's just for a little bit! It'll be fine!

1873
00:12:26,747 --> 00:12:30,277
Yay! I get to see Maria! Let's go!

1874
00:12:30,277 --> 00:12:32,097
Sister, calm down!

1875
00:12:46,667 --> 00:12:48,887
Mom, is there anything I can do?

1876
00:12:48,887 --> 00:12:51,557
Oh... Could you go on a shopping run for me?

1877
00:12:51,557 --> 00:12:52,377
Sure.

1878
00:12:56,587 --> 00:12:59,387
Wow... So this is Maria's town, huh?

1879
00:12:59,387 --> 00:13:02,407
Sister, you don't even know
 where her house is, do you?

1880
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:04,597
Oh, come to think of it, I don't.

1881
00:13:05,087 --> 00:13:09,097
Excuse me! Do you know where 
Maria Campbell-san lives?

1882
00:13:09,257 --> 00:13:12,727
Maria Campbell? Yes, of course I know.

1883
00:13:12,727 --> 00:13:15,017
Maria's quite popular in this town.

1884
00:13:15,137 --> 00:13:17,487
Popular? Really?

1885
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:20,787
She's been an extraordinary girl 
ever since she was little.

1886
00:13:20,787 --> 00:13:23,917
She's a commoner with light magic, after all.

1887
00:13:24,557 --> 00:13:27,997
You're right. She's very special, isn't she?

1888
00:13:28,137 --> 00:13:30,977
To get to the Campbells' house, 
just follow this street,

1889
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:32,497
and when you're past the trees...

1890
00:13:36,817 --> 00:13:39,747
This is such a lovely, peaceful place.

1891
00:13:39,747 --> 00:13:40,607
Yeah.

1892
00:13:40,607 --> 00:13:41,587
You there!

1893
00:13:42,967 --> 00:13:44,827
Are you a friend of Maria's?

1894
00:13:44,827 --> 00:13:48,597
Then you must know, right? 
Who is Maria's real father?

1895
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:49,757
Huh?

1896
00:13:49,757 --> 00:13:51,307
Her real father?

1897
00:13:51,307 --> 00:13:53,897
Come on, now. Don't pretend you don't know.

1898
00:13:53,897 --> 00:13:56,797
Her real father is a noble, isn't he?

1899
00:13:56,797 --> 00:13:58,857
That's why she can use light magic!

1900
00:13:59,697 --> 00:14:02,487
Um... I'm not sure what you—

1901
00:14:02,487 --> 00:14:04,137
She's a noble's illegitimate child, right?!

1902
00:14:04,137 --> 00:14:06,997
It's no wonder her family fell apart!

1903
00:14:09,697 --> 00:14:11,387
We're in a hurry.

1904
00:14:11,737 --> 00:14:14,417
You'll have to excuse us, ladies.

1905
00:14:19,467 --> 00:14:22,907
Gosh, Keith, there was no need 
to take off running...

1906
00:14:22,907 --> 00:14:25,097
Don't worry about what they said.

1907
00:14:25,097 --> 00:14:27,327
Rumors are only rumors.

1908
00:14:29,927 --> 00:14:32,387
That must be the Campbells' house.

1909
00:14:43,617 --> 00:14:45,267
Hello!

1910
00:14:49,467 --> 00:14:51,157
May I ask who's calling?

1911
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:55,227
I'm Maria-san's friend. 
My name is Catarina Claes.

1912
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:56,657
I'm her brother, Keith.

1913
00:14:56,787 --> 00:14:58,917
Friends of Maria's?

1914
00:14:59,177 --> 00:15:01,257
Is Maria-san home?

1915
00:15:01,257 --> 00:15:03,787
I'm sorry to say she isn't right now.

1916
00:15:04,207 --> 00:15:06,677
Would you like to wait for her inside?

1917
00:15:06,677 --> 00:15:08,257
Thank you!

1918
00:15:08,977 --> 00:15:09,977
Here you go.

1919
00:15:10,317 --> 00:15:13,587
Wow! Did Maria-san make these?

1920
00:15:13,587 --> 00:15:16,707
What? Ah, no... These were purchased.

1921
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:19,217
Oh... I'm sorry.

1922
00:15:19,217 --> 00:15:21,737
I thought perhaps she had made them.

1923
00:15:21,737 --> 00:15:24,057
She always shares her 
homemade sweets with me.

1924
00:15:24,057 --> 00:15:27,537
What? She's been making sweets?

1925
00:15:27,537 --> 00:15:30,617
Yes! They're really delicious, aren't they?

1926
00:15:31,267 --> 00:15:32,087
Huh?

1927
00:15:33,417 --> 00:15:34,747
Yes...

1928
00:15:34,747 --> 00:15:35,827
I'm back.

1929
00:15:36,147 --> 00:15:39,437
Catarina-sama and Keith-sama? 
What are you doing here?

1930
00:15:40,377 --> 00:15:41,267
Here we are!

1931
00:15:41,267 --> 00:15:43,127
We apologize for coming over unannounced.

1932
00:15:43,237 --> 00:15:46,757
No... I'm happy to see you on our day off!

1933
00:15:50,427 --> 00:15:52,737
I-I'm sorry...

1934
00:15:52,737 --> 00:15:55,847
I suddenly felt hungry 
the moment I saw your face.

1935
00:15:56,537 --> 00:15:59,507
Since you're here, 
why don't I make some sweets?

1936
00:15:59,507 --> 00:16:02,087
You will?! Yay!

1937
00:16:02,087 --> 00:16:04,997
In that case, I don't know 
if you could call it a favor in return,

1938
00:16:04,997 --> 00:16:07,527
but would you mind 
if I borrowed your field for a bit?

1939
00:16:07,527 --> 00:16:08,157
What?

1940
00:16:08,157 --> 00:16:09,407
Sister!

1941
00:16:09,527 --> 00:16:13,267
Working fields is actually a hobby of mine.

1942
00:16:13,267 --> 00:16:16,367
And I brought some great seedlings 
that I just got my hands on!

1943
00:16:16,607 --> 00:16:19,707
I never knew you had a hobby like that...

1944
00:16:20,017 --> 00:16:22,337
Of course, I don't mind.

1945
00:16:22,337 --> 00:16:24,307
Thank you!

1946
00:16:31,127 --> 00:16:34,917
I'm sure Catarina-sama 
is going to be very hungry.

1947
00:16:35,747 --> 00:16:37,547
I'll have to make lots.

1948
00:16:45,377 --> 00:16:46,307
Here.

1949
00:16:59,017 --> 00:17:02,077
<i>I was the kind of normal child you'd see anywhere.</i>

1950
00:17:17,097 --> 00:17:21,057
<i>But after my light magic became 
active, everything changed.</i>

1951
00:17:21,427 --> 00:17:24,637
<i>There are very few 
commoners who possess magic.</i>

1952
00:17:24,637 --> 00:17:30,037
<i>Everyone avoided me and suspected 
that I was a noble's illegitimate child.</i>

1953
00:17:34,967 --> 00:17:39,347
<i>I tried my best to regain my former happiness.</i>

1954
00:17:39,347 --> 00:17:43,667
<i>I worked my hardest to not let 
it all be blamed on my magic.</i>

1955
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:49,387
<i>Before I knew it, I was drawing 
everyone's attention as a "special child."</i>

1956
00:17:50,077 --> 00:17:53,457
<i>But in the end, nothing changed.</i>

1957
00:17:54,297 --> 00:17:57,427
<i>What must I do to make them see me?</i>

1958
00:18:29,107 --> 00:18:33,207
<i>I just wished that someone, 
anyone, would look at me...</i>

1959
00:18:33,927 --> 00:18:35,777
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

1960
00:18:42,307 --> 00:18:46,117
<i>After that day, Maria stopped making sweets.</i>

1961
00:18:47,217 --> 00:18:49,627
<i>I couldn't say anything to her.</i>

1962
00:18:50,067 --> 00:18:52,367
<i>I was too wrapped up in my own problems.</i>

1963
00:18:52,967 --> 00:18:55,567
<i>I couldn't even look at my own daughter.</i>

1964
00:18:56,277 --> 00:18:58,617
<i>What a cruel mother I am...</i>

1965
00:19:00,907 --> 00:19:02,947
<i>I'm still the same as I was then,</i>

1966
00:19:03,907 --> 00:19:05,717
<i>but Maria...</i>

1967
00:19:43,147 --> 00:19:45,027
Use these.

1968
00:19:48,207 --> 00:19:49,957
I remember these!

1969
00:19:50,207 --> 00:19:51,387
I'll help you.

1970
00:20:09,507 --> 00:20:11,527
Let's dig in!

1971
00:20:12,807 --> 00:20:14,157
They're delicious!

1972
00:20:14,787 --> 00:20:16,277
I'm so glad.

1973
00:20:16,277 --> 00:20:18,867
Maria makes the best sweets ever!

1974
00:20:18,867 --> 00:20:19,607
Indeed!

1975
00:20:19,607 --> 00:20:21,117
Thank you so much.

1976
00:20:26,097 --> 00:20:31,447
Thank you for tidying up our field so nicely.

1977
00:20:31,447 --> 00:20:34,107
It was no problem at all.
Thank you for the sweets and tea.

1978
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:37,307
You'll have to look forward to 
finding out what'll grow in that field.

1979
00:20:37,977 --> 00:20:40,207
Please come visit again sometime.

1980
00:20:40,207 --> 00:20:41,877
I'd love to.

1981
00:20:41,877 --> 00:20:42,767
Goodbye..

1982
00:20:43,867 --> 00:20:44,947
Um...

1983
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:49,627
Please continue to be 
a good friend to my daughter.

1984
00:20:54,397 --> 00:20:56,037
Of course!

1985
00:20:56,037 --> 00:20:58,527
And thank you for giving me your blessing!

1986
00:21:20,627 --> 00:21:23,297
This has been a fantastic day!

1987
00:21:23,297 --> 00:21:26,337
I sort of wish I could see our mother now.

1988
00:21:26,337 --> 00:21:28,137
Shall we stop by on our way, then?

1989
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:31,787
Mother!

1990
00:21:31,787 --> 00:21:33,657
Sister, your outfit—

1991
00:21:36,027 --> 00:21:38,237
Welcome home, Catarina.

1992
00:21:38,237 --> 00:21:41,377
What an unusual outfit you're wearing.

1993
00:21:41,377 --> 00:21:44,457
Well, you can tell me all about that later.

1994
00:21:45,047 --> 00:21:48,287
I heard a strange rumor at a tea party 
for the ladies' association.

1995
00:21:48,587 --> 00:21:50,497
A... A strange rumor?

1996
00:21:52,097 --> 00:21:55,277
Rumor says that someone had 
started a farm, of all things,

1997
00:21:55,277 --> 00:21:59,387
on the venerable magic academy grounds.

1998
00:22:02,377 --> 00:22:06,977
Catarina, why don't we have 
a little chat in my room?

